From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5cemu <ps5cemu@localhost>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 04:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: folders anyone can write

Azahar made its folders 0755: the 3DS's storage, each installed title's
folders in sdmc, the shader cache's. The app runs as root when the HEN
jailbreaks it and as its own user when it needs no HEN, and the
console's FTP service runs as another user still, so what one of them
made the others could not write: a game whose saves and shader cache
could not be written started to a black screen (#55), and installed
titles could not be deleted over FTP or from a file manager (#58).
CreateDir makes them 0777 on the PS5, as the port's own folders are (its
umask is 0, so the files Azahar writes are 0666).
---
 src/common/file_util.cpp | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/common/file_util.cpp b/src/common/file_util.cpp
index 3168a26..efe7a48 100644
--- a/src/common/file_util.cpp
+++ b/src/common/file_util.cpp
@@ -328,7 +328,16 @@ bool CreateDir(const std::string& path) {
     }
 
 #else
-    if (mkdir(path.c_str(), 0755) == 0)
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    // Anyone's to write, as the port's own folders are (its umask is 0): the app runs as root with
+    // the HEN's jailbreak and as its own user without, and the console's FTP service as another,
+    // and a folder one of them made 0755 kept the others out: a game's saves and shader cache
+    // (#55), installed titles no file manager could delete (#58)
+    constexpr mode_t mode = 0777;
+#else
+    constexpr mode_t mode = 0755;
+#endif
+    if (mkdir(path.c_str(), mode) == 0)
         return true;
 
     int err = errno;
